2026-10-22T17:05:30 The text leading up to this was:
2026-10-22T17:05:31 --------------------------
2026-10-22T17:05:31 |From openbsd-tech Sun May 16 22:30:39 2021
2026-10-22T17:05:32 |From: Andrew Hewus Fresh <andrew () afresh1 ! com>
2026-10-22T17:05:32 |Date: Sun, 16 May 2021 22:30:39 +0000
2026-10-22T17:05:32 |To: openbsd-tech
2026-10-22T17:05:33 |Subject: Add versioned lib to system perl's @INC for non-packaged modules
2026-10-22T17:05:33 |Message-Id: <20210516223039.GF34579 () us ! holligan ! net>
2026-10-22T17:05:34 |X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-tech&m=162120435916828
2026-10-22T17:05:34 |
2026-10-22T17:05:34 |This patch is should make it easier to recover from problems that happen
2026-10-22T17:05:35 |when installing perl modules outside of the package system. You might
2026-10-22T17:05:35 |recognize the "loadable library and perl binaries are mismatched" error.
2026-10-22T17:05:35 |
2026-10-22T17:05:36 |Adding a versioned subdirectory for cpan modules means that when the
2026-10-22T17:05:36 |perl version changes it will no longer find those old modules and it
2026-10-22T17:05:37 |will be easy to remove them without disturbing things from packages.
2026-10-22T17:05:37 |
2026-10-22T17:05:37 |Only slightly related, but we can avoid breaking base tools like pkg_add
2026-10-22T17:05:38 |and friend by using "no lib '/usr/local/libdata/perl5/site_perl';" to
2026-10-22T17:05:38 |avoid looking in those directories at all.
2026-10-22T17:05:38 |
2026-10-22T17:05:39 |
2026-10-22T17:05:39 |The new @INC looks like this. The first "5.32.1" sitelib is where
2026-10-22T17:05:40 |external things, like cpan(1), will install. The current "site_perl"
2026-10-22T17:05:40 |directory (now vendorlib) will continue to be where ports/packages go.
2026-10-22T17:05:40 |Finally, "/usr/libdata" privlib is for things that ship with the base
2026-10-22T17:05:41 |system.
2026-10-22T17:05:41 |
2026-10-22T17:05:42 |$ perl -V | perl -ne 'print if /INC/..eof'
2026-10-22T17:05:42 | @INC:
2026-10-22T17:05:42 | /usr/local/libdata/perl5/site_perl/5.32.1/sparc64-openbsd
2026-10-22T17:05:42 | /usr/local/libdata/perl5/site_perl/5.32.1
2026-10-22T17:05:43 | /usr/local/libdata/perl5/site_perl/sparc64-openbsd
2026-10-22T17:05:43 | /usr/local/libdata/perl5/site_perl
2026-10-22T17:05:44 | /usr/libdata/perl5/sparc64-openbsd
2026-10-22T17:05:44 | /usr/libdata/perl5
2026-10-22T17:05:44 |
2026-10-22T17:05:45 |
2026-10-22T17:05:45 |One place this might cause temporary issues in the ports tree is
2026-10-22T17:05:45 |anything that doesn't use the overrides in perl.port.mk and looks up
2026-10-22T17:05:46 |sitelib itself. It should be fairly obvious as it should fail to
2026-10-22T17:05:46 |package because the files in the PLIST will not exist (they'll be in the
2026-10-22T17:05:46 |versioned subdir). I didn't run into that in my testing, but I didn't
2026-10-22T17:05:47 |complete a full bulk build.
2026-10-22T17:05:47 |
2026-10-22T17:05:47 |There do appear to be some annoyances with still shared directories for
2026-10-22T17:05:48 |man pages, in that if you install a CPAN module and then attempt to
2026-10-22T17:05:48 |pkg_add it, it complains because "files already exist" in the man
2026-10-22T17:05:48 |directory. We could separate the cpan man pages, or I think un-setting
2026-10-22T17:05:49 |the site_lib man*dir will mean cpan won't instal them. I haven't yet
2026-10-22T17:05:49 |tested that, but I'm not sure what would be best there.
2026-10-22T17:05:50 |
2026-10-22T17:05:50 |
2026-10-22T17:05:51 |Unfortunately I did do a bunch of testing of different ways to add
2026-10-22T17:05:51 |things to @INC which meant this patch also does some reorganization of
2026-10-22T17:05:51 |the contents, I can turn it into a smaller patch if requested and do the
2026-10-22T17:05:51 |cleanup separately.
2026-10-22T17:05:52 |
2026-10-22T17:05:52 |
2026-10-22T17:05:52 |Comments, OK? Should I see if sthen@ will do a full bulk build first?
2026-10-22T17:05:53 |
2026-10-22T17:05:53 |
