2026-10-22T17:06:53 --------------------------
2026-10-22T17:06:53 |========================================================================
2026-10-22T17:06:54 |CVE-2026-15534 CPAN Security Group
2026-10-22T17:06:54 |========================================================================
2026-10-22T17:06:54 |
2026-10-22T17:06:54 | CVE ID: CVE-2026-15534
2026-10-22T17:06:55 | Distribution: perl
2026-10-22T17:06:55 | Versions: through 5.45.1
2026-10-22T17:06:55 |
2026-10-22T17:06:56 | MetaCPAN: https://metacpan.org/dist/perl
2026-10-22T17:06:56 | VCS Repo: https://github.com/Perl/perl5
2026-10-22T17:06:56 |
2026-10-22T17:06:56 |Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes
2026-10-22T17:06:57 |during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache
2026-10-22T17:06:57 |in S_regmatch
2026-10-22T17:06:57 |
2026-10-22T17:06:57 |Description
2026-10-22T17:06:58 |-----------
2026-10-22T17:06:58 |Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes
2026-10-22T17:06:58 |during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache
2026-10-22T17:06:58 |in S_regmatch.
2026-10-22T17:06:58 |
2026-10-22T17:06:59 |The regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position
2026-10-22T17:06:59 |for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject
2026-10-22T17:06:59 |length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product
2026-10-22T17:07:00 |for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte
2026-10-22T17:07:00 |subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores
2026-10-22T17:07:00 |the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed
2026-10-22T17:07:00 |from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end
2026-10-22T17:07:00 |of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.
2026-10-22T17:07:01 |
2026-10-22T17:07:01 |A caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size
2026-10-22T17:07:01 |against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap
2026-10-22T17:07:02 |memory.
2026-10-22T17:07:02 |
2026-10-22T17:07:02 |Problem types
2026-10-22T17:07:03 |-------------
2026-10-22T17:07:03 |- CWE-190 Integer Overflow or Wraparound
2026-10-22T17:07:03 |- CWE-125 Out-of-bounds Read
2026-10-22T17:07:03 |- CWE-787 Out-of-bounds Write
2026-10-22T17:07:04 |
2026-10-22T17:07:04 |Solutions
2026-10-22T17:07:04 |---------
2026-10-22T17:07:04 |Upgrade to a future Perl release, or apply the upstream patches.
2026-10-22T17:07:05 |
2026-10-22T17:07:05 |References
2026-10-22T17:07:05 |----------
2026-10-22T17:07:06 |https://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/42536248/
2026-10-22T17:07:06 |https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/568e6fd238867bb9e99fa3f47cba3169009239e0.patch
2026-10-22T17:07:06 |https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/54cf3d44cbbedd17d774e9a37921963e8fd5d0cb.patch
2026-10-22T17:07:06 |
2026-10-22T17:07:07 |
2026-10-22T17:07:07 |From 54cf3d44cbbedd17d774e9a37921963e8fd5d0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
2026-10-22T17:07:07 |From: David Mitchell <davem@iabyn.com>
2026-10-22T17:07:07 |Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 12:14:52 +0100
2026-10-22T17:07:08 |Subject: [PATCH] regex: make superlinear cache 64-bit clean
2026-10-22T17:07:08 |
2026-10-22T17:07:08 |(See the previous commit for an explanation of what the SLC is).
2026-10-22T17:07:09 |
2026-10-22T17:07:09 |The iter and maxiter variables associated with the SLC are currently
2026-10-22T17:07:09 |declared as I32. This causes various possible issues, including
2026-10-22T17:07:09 |potential out of bounds reads and writes of the cache in the presence of
2026-10-22T17:07:10 |very large strings and many WHILEM nodes: for example when the string is
2026-10-22T17:07:10 |over 128Mb and there are 16 nodes (the max).
2026-10-22T17:07:10 |
2026-10-22T17:07:11 |Following on from the previous commit which made iter never be negative,
2026-10-22T17:07:11 |this commit changes the variables' type to STRLEN (typically equal to
2026-10-22T17:07:11 |U64 on 64-bit systems) and does calculations in a way to avoid potential
2026-10-22T17:07:11 |overflows. If an overflow *could* occur, the cache isn't enabled.
2026-10-22T17:07:11 |
2026-10-22T17:07:12 |Previously, a -ve overflow was "fixed" by setting maxiter to I32_MAX, and
2026-10-22T17:07:12 |+ve overflows weren't detected.
2026-10-22T17:07:12 |
2026-10-22T17:07:13 |No tests are added, since this code only affects very large strings
2026-10-22T17:07:13 |using lots of memory and iterations, and such tests would crash on small
2026-10-22T17:07:13 |memory machines.
2026-10-22T17:07:13 |---
2026-10-22T17:07:14 | regexec.c | 23 ++++++++++++++---------
2026-10-22T17:07:14 | regexp.h | 4 ++--
2026-10-22T17:07:14 | 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
2026-10-22T17:07:14 |
2026-10-22T17:07:15 |diff --git a/regexec.c b/regexec.c
2026-10-22T17:07:15 |index 29aa73c13cb9..66e0c0924059 100644
2026-10-22T17:07:15 |--- ./regexec.c.orig Mon Jun 22 07:48:00 2026
2026-10-22T17:07:15 |+++ ./regexec.c Tue Aug 18 23:15:52 2026
2026-10-22T17:07:16 --------------------------
